THE TOKENS WENT WITH IT
--landing-slab, --landing-on-slab, --landing-brass-on-slab and --landing-muted-on-slab
existed only for this band; grep confirmed no other reference. Two of them were added in
Phase 1 specifically to fix contrast failures on it. Leaving them would have left dead
colour behind elaborate comments describing a band that no longer exists, so they were
removed in both themes along with the comments justifying them.

CONSEQUENCE FOR THE DARK THEME
This was the page's only dark band, and NFR1 was written around it inverting — sitting
0.850 below paper in light and 0.105 above it in dark. That inversion still holds for the
warm band (-0.049 -> +0.049) and the footer (-0.018 -> +0.018), so the mechanism is
unchanged, but the drama is gone. The page now runs paper, warm, paper, paper, brass CTA,
light footer, which makes the brass CTA the only saturated moment. Calmer than the
prototype, and consistent with product-guidelines.md's 'calm, precise, never breathless'.
NFR1 and the token comments were rewritten to describe what the page actually does rather
than leaving a rationale that pointed at a deleted section.

